@style verse
  Inscribed to a dear Child:
  in memory of golden summer hours
  and whispers of a summer sea.

@style verse
  Girt with a boyish garb for boyish task,
  [aki 2zw]Eager she wields her spade: yet loves as well
  Rest on a friendly knee, intent to ask
  [aki 2zw]The tale he loves to tell.

@style verse
  Rude spirits of the seething outer strife,
  [aki 2zw]Unmeet to read her pure and simple spright,
  Deem, if you list, such hours a waste of life,
  [aki 2zw]Empty of all delight!

@style verse
  Chat on, sweet Maid, and rescue from annoy
  [aki 2zw]Hearts that by wiser talk are unbeguiled.
  Ah, happy he who owns that tenderest joy,
  [aki 2zw]The heart-love of a child!

@style verse
  Away, fond thoughts, and vex my soul no more!
  [aki 2zw]Work claims my wakeful nights, my busy days—
  Albeit bright memories of that sunlit shore
  [aki 2zw]Yet haunt my dreaming gaze!

