  “The method employed I would gladly explain,
  [aki 2.5zw]While I have it so clear in my head,
  If I had but the time and you had but the brain—
  [aki 2.5zw]But much yet remains to be said.

@style verse
  “In one moment I’ve seen what has hitherto been
  [aki 2.5zw]Enveloped in absolute mystery,
  And without extra charge I will give you at large
  [aki 2.5zw]A Lesson in Natural History.”

@style verse
  In his genial way he proceeded to say
  [aki 2.5zw](Forgetting all laws of propriety,
  And that giving instruction, without introduction,
  [aki 2.5zw]Would have caused quite a thrill in Society),

@style verse
  “As to temper the Jubjub’s a desperate bird,
  [aki 2.5zw]Since it lives in perpetual passion:
  Its taste in costume is entirely absurd—
  [aki 2.5zw]It is ages ahead of the fashion:

@style verse
  “But it knows any friend it has met once before:
  [aki 2.5zw]It never will look at a bribe:
  And in charity-meetings it stands at the door,
  [aki 2.5zw]And collects—though it does not subscribe.

@style verse
  “Its’ flavour when cooked is more exquisite far
  [aki 2.5zw]Than mutton, or oysters, or eggs:
  (Some think it keeps best in an ivory jar,
  [aki 2.5zw]And some, in mahogany kegs:)

@style verse
  “You boil it in sawdust: you salt it in glue:
  [aki 2.5zw]You condense it with locusts and tape:
  Still keeping one principal object in view—
  [aki 2.5zw]To preserve its symmetrical shape.”

@style verse
  The Butcher would gladly have talked till next day,
  [aki 2.5zw]But he felt that the lesson must end,
  And he wept with delight in attempting to say
  [aki 2.5zw]He considered the Beaver his friend.

@style verse
  While the Beaver confessed, with affectionate looks
  [aki 2.5zw]More eloquent even than tears,
  It had learned in ten minutes far more than all books
  [aki 2.5zw]Would have taught it in seventy years.

@style verse
  They returned hand-in-hand, and the Bellman, unmanned
  [aki 2.5zw](For a moment) with noble emotion,
  Said “This amply repays all the wearisome days
  [aki 2.5zw]We have spent on the billowy ocean!”

@style verse
  Such friends, as the Beaver and Butcher became,
  [aki 2.5zw]Have seldom if ever been known;
  In winter or summer, ’twas always the same—
  [aki 2.5zw]You could never meet either alone.

@style verse
  And when quarrels arose—as one frequently finds
  [aki 2.5zw]Quarrels will, spite of every endeavour—
  The song of the Jubjub recurred to their minds,
  [aki 2.5zw]And cemented their friendship for ever!

