## THE BANKER’S FATE

@style verse
  They sought it with thimbles, they sought it with care;
  [aki 2.5zw]They pursued it with forks and hope;
  They threatened its life with a railway-share;
  [aki 2.5zw]They charmed it with smiles and soap.

@style verse
  And the Banker, inspired with a courage so new
  [aki 2.5zw]It was matter for general remark,
  Rushed madly ahead and was lost to their view
  [aki 2.5zw]In his zeal to discover the Snark

@style verse
  But while he was seeking with thimbles and care,
  [aki 2.5zw]A Bandersnatch swiftly drew nigh
  And grabbed at the Banker, who shrieked in despair,
  [aki 2.5zw]For he knew it was useless to fly.

@style verse
  He offered large discount—he offered a cheque
  [aki 2.5zw](Drawn “to bearer”) for seven-pounds-ten:
  But the Bandersnatch merely extended its neck
  [aki 2.5zw]And grabbed at the Banker again.

@style verse
  Without rest or pause—while those frumious jaws
  [aki 2.5zw]Went savagely snapping around—
  He skipped and he hopped, and he floundered and flopped,
  [aki 2.5zw]Till fainting he fell to the ground.

@style verse
  The Bandersnatch fled as the others appeared
  [aki 2.5zw]Led on by that fear-stricken yell:
  And the Bellman remarked “It is just as I feared!”
  [aki 3zw]And solemnly tolled on his bell.

@style verse
  He was black in the face, and they scarcely could trace
  [aki 2.5zw]The least likeness to what he had been:
  While so great was his fright that his waistcoat turned white—
  [aki 2.5zw]A wonderful thing to be seen!

@style verse
  To the horror of all who were present that day.
  [aki 2.5zw]He uprose in full evening dress,
  And with senseless grimaces endeavoured to say
  [aki 2.5zw]What his tongue could no longer express.

@style verse
  Down he sank in a chair—ran his hands through his hair—
  [aki 2.5zw]And chanted in mimsiest tones
  Words whose utter inanity proved his insanity,
  [aki 2.5zw]While he rattled a couple of bones.

@style verse
  “Leave him here to his fate—it is getting so late!”
  [aki 3zw]The Bellman exclaimed in a fright.
  “We have lost half the day. Any further delay,
  [aki 2.5zw]And we sha’n’t catch a Snark before night!”

