@nonumber
## THE VANISHING

@style verse
  They sought it with thimbles, they sought it with care;
  [aki 2.5zw]They pursued it with forks and hope;
  They threatened its life with a railway-share;
  [aki 2.5zw]They charmed it with smiles and soap.

@style verse
  They shuddered to think that the chase might fail,
  [aki 2.5zw]And the Beaver, excited at last,
  Went bounding along on the tip of its tail,
  [aki 2.5zw]For the daylight was nearly past.

@style verse
  “There is Thingumbob shouting!” the Bellman said,
  [aki 2.5zw]“He is shouting like mad, only hark!
  He is waving his hands, he is wagging his head,
  [aki 2.5zw]He has certainly found a Snark!”

@style verse
  They gazed in delight, while the Butcher exclaimed
  [aki 2.5zw]“He was always a desperate wag!”
  [aki 0.5zw]They beheld him—their Baker—their hero unnamed—
  [aki 2.5zw]On the top of a neighboring crag.

@style verse
  Erect and sublime, for one moment of time.
  [aki 2.5zw]In the next, that wild figure they saw
  (As if stung by a spasm) plunge into a chasm,
  [aki 2.5zw]While they waited and listened in awe.

@style verse
  “It’s a Snark!” was the sound that first came to their ears,
  [aki 2.5zw]And seemed almost too good to be true.
  Then followed a torrent of laughter and cheers:
  [aki 2.5zw]Then the ominous words “It’s a Boo-”

@style verse
  Then, silence. Some fancied they heard in the air
  [aki 2.5zw]A weary and wandering sigh
  Then sounded like “-jum!” but the others declare
  [aki 2.5zw]It was only a breeze that went by.

@style verse
  They hunted till darkness came on, but they found
  [aki 2.5zw]Not a button, or feather, or mark,
  By which they could tell that they stood on the ground
  [aki 2.5zw]Where the Baker had met with the Snark.

@style verse
  In the midst of the word he was trying to say,
  [aki 2.5zw]In the midst of his laughter and glee,
  He had softly and suddenly vanished away—-
  [aki 2.5zw]For the Snark [italic: was] a Boojum, you see.

